[HEADING=1]XenForo 2.3.13 — PHP 8.2 → 8.6 Web Stack Benchmark[/HEADING]

[B]Four stacks, five PHP versions, guest and logged-in traffic, on two independent servers.[/B]

[HEADING=2]TL;DR[/HEADING]

[TABLE]
[TR]
[TH]Question[/TH]
[TH]Answer[/TH]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD]Biggest performance win[/TD]
[TD][B]Angie [ICODE]fastcgi_cache[/ICODE] guest-page cache[/B]: [B]88×–180×[/B] more guest requests/s[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD]Fastest stack overall[/TD]
[TD][B]Stack 3 — Valkey + Angie page cache[/B] (guest-heavy forum)[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD]Fastest stack for logged-in users[/TD]
[TD][B]Stack 1 — plain Angie + PHP + MariaDB[/B] (no Valkey, no page cache)[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD]Does Valkey data caching help a single server?[/TD]
[TD][B]No.[/B] It costs [B]2–14 %[/B] versus plain; Credis and phpredis measured the same[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD]Cost of Anubis[/TD]
[TD][B]−90…−94 %[/B] on cached guest pages, [B]−17…−19 %[/B] on dynamic/member pages[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD]PHP 8.6 vs 8.2[/TD]
[TD][B]+0…+3 %[/B] at low concurrency; [B]≤1.5 %[/B] at saturation — no meaningful gain[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD]PHP version ranking[/TD]
[TD][B]8.6 RC5 > 8.5 > 8.4 ≈ 8.2 > 8.3[/B] (differences are small)[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD]PHP 8.6 without [ICODE]php-redis[/ICODE][/TD]
[TD]Works with [B]SV/RedisCache + bundled Credis[/B]; all add-ons active, all tiers HTTP 200[/TD]
[/TR]
[/TABLE]


