[HEADING=2]Method[/HEADING]

[LIST]
[*]Loopback HTTPS against [ICODE]xf.test.local[/ICODE], self-signed certificate.
[*][ICODE]wrk -t4 -c100 -d10s[/ICODE], 2 s warm-up, per tier.
[*][B]Guest cached:[/B] [ICODE]GET /[/ICODE] with no cookies.
[*][B]Guest bypass:[/B] [ICODE]GET /[/ICODE] with [ICODE]Cookie: xf_session=bench-bypass[/ICODE] (bypasses the guest cache without logging in).
[*][B]Member home:[/B] [ICODE]GET /[/ICODE] with a valid XenForo session cookie.
[*][B]Member thread:[/B] a seeded 100k-post thread with the same session cookie.
[*]The FastCGI cache was cleared before each PHP version; Valkey DB 1 was flushed when the data cache was toggled.
[*]The active PHP version was verified with a [ICODE]PHP_VERSION[/ICODE] probe on every run (the first attempt exposed a stale Anubis connection pool serving the previous PHP version; the final runs force a restart on version changes).
[*]Low-concurrency efficiency: [ICODE]wrk -t2 -c8 -d15s[/ICODE], [B]3 runs averaged[/B], plain stack.
[/LIST]

[QUOTE]The four stack passes ran sequentially. Small differences between Stack 1 and Stack 2 (a few percent) are within run-order/thermal drift; the page-cache and Anubis effects are far larger than that drift.[/QUOTE]


